   "Discharge Summary",
   "Hospital Medicine",
   "D. Lusk, MD",
   "72 M admitted 08/09 with new AF RVR 140s, mild pulmonary edema, BNP 412. Rate controlled with IV diltiazem then PO diltiazem + metoprolol. Echo EF 50-55%, LA dilated. TSH nl. Trop flat. CHA2DS2-VASc 3. Started warfarin 08/10 (pt preferred over DOAC due to cost/coverage), enoxaparin bridge until INR therapeutic. Discharged on metoprolol succinate 50, diltiazem ER 180, warfarin 5 mg. F/u anticoag clinic 3 days, cardiology 2 wk."
